# NOTE on verifying this block: `git check-ignore -v <path>` exits 0 for ANY
# matching pattern, negations included (see its own docs: "0 - One or more
# of the provided paths is ignored" — that wording covers a negation match
# too). A `!`-prefixed pattern in the -v output means the path is NOT
# excluded, but the exit code alone does not show that. To verify a
# negation actually re-includes a path, use `git status --ignored=matching`
# (untracked+non-ignored is `??`, ignored is `!!`) or `git add -n <path>`.

